<title>USA: Intermet files with SEC for 3 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Intermet files with SEC for 3 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intermet Corp filed Friday with the U.S.  Securities and Exchange Commission for an offering of up to three  million shares to be sold by a group of shareholders.</p>
<p>The offering's underwriters -- Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette Securities  Corp, Prudential Securities Inc and Interstate/Johnson Lane Corp --  have an over-allotment option of up to 450,000 shares.</p>
<p>Intermet, with headquarters in Troy, Michigan, is an independent producer  of ductile iron castings.</p>
</text>
